/-!
# Reductions for the marked four-cover center action and lifting defect

The marked field and diagonal elements generate the full center action once
the diagonal moves Z(L). The source specialization proves that movement from
Z(L) <= YS. An intrinsic nonidentity central twist supplies the literal lifting
defect while preserving the original elements.

For arbitrary NormalizerGeometry, the unconditional diagonal movement and a
nonidentity intrinsic twist remain model calculations. Neither is assumed as
an additional field of the cover or claimed as an unconditional theorem here.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith 15.3.38, printed pp.1136--1137.
-/
